# rag_ablation — does the codebase indexer actually ground the dev agent?
# Each goal asks the LIVE DevAgent to explain a real repo file. `anchor_terms` are
# real identifiers/terms from that file. --mode ablation runs every goal WITH the
# CodebaseIndexer wired and WITHOUT it, and scores anchor-term recall for each; the
# headline is mean Δ (with − without). A grounded answer surfaces these symbols; a
# hallucinated one ("quantum circuit execution jobs" for the scheduler) does not.
# Read-only goals only; the run executes real plans, so it's Tier-2 / on-demand.
{"id": "ab-scheduler", "suite": "rag_ablation", "goal": "explain what core/scheduler.py does", "anchor_terms": ["AccessibilityScheduler", "fan_out", "semaphore", "priority", "DEV_AGENT"], "tags": ["explain", "rag"]}
